      <h2>Safety</h2>

      <div class="warning">
        <strong>Read and understand the entire owner&rsquo;s manual before attempting assembly or operation.</strong> This lathe is intended for properly trained and experienced users only.
      </div>

      <ul>
        <li>Wear ANSI Z87.1 safety glasses with side shields. Wear hearing protection if noise exceeds safe levels. Do not wear gloves.</li>
        <li>Remove ties, rings, watches and jewelry; roll sleeves above the elbows; confine long hair; no loose clothing.</li>
        <li>Make sure the switch is OFF before plugging in. Unplug before adjusting, servicing, or cleaning. Clean chips with a brush or compressed air, not your hands.</li>
        <li>Remove adjusting keys and wrenches before starting. Keep guards in place.</li>
        <li>Inspect every workpiece for cracks, checks, knots and other defects. Defective stock can break apart and cause serious injury.</li>
        <li>Secure the workpiece properly in the chuck, on the faceplate, or between centers. Rotate it by hand to check clearance from the tool rest and machine before starting.</li>
        <li>Stand to one side when starting. Start at low speed and let the lathe ramp up.</li>
        <li>Position the tool rest close to the work and at proper height. Adjust only with power off.</li>
        <li>Keep hands away from rotating stock. Never stop a rotating workpiece with your hand.</li>
        <li>Never leave the lathe running unattended. Do not stand on the machine.</li>
        <li>Keep turning tools sharp. Use quality glue appropriate to the work when gluing up blanks.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Switch Lockout</h3>
      <p>A padlock (not provided) can be fitted to the ON/OFF switch atop the inverter to prevent unauthorized use. Push the switch to OFF, insert the padlock through the holes, and lock it.</p>
